# Location-first business search

When changing OpenAI / Places / mission planning code:

- NEVER look up a restaurant or business by brand name alone.
- ALWAYS pass `profile.area`, `profile.latitude`, and `profile.longitude` into search.
- Prefer the nearest location within ~20–25 miles; reject hours-away franchise hits (e.g. Prosper when user is in Liberty Hill).
- See root `AGENTS.md` and `backend/src/services/location.js`.

# Pickup orders need items first

- "call X and make a pickup order" with no menu items → ask what to order before dialing.
- Do not use the direct-call shortcut for restaurant pickup/order placement.
- See `needsOrderItemsBeforeCall` in `backend/src/services/openai.js` and `AGENTS.md`.

# Stay on live calls

- If the callee is unclear, ask them to repeat/clarify — do not hang up mid-call.
- See AGENTS.md "Stay on the line" and `buildMissionCallPrompt` in `backend/src/services/vapi.js`.

# Human greeting on outbound calls

- We say Hi first. ~5s silence (Vapi min) → "Can you hear me?" Once they speak, reply immediately (no dead air).
- Do not volunteer "this is {name}" unless asked (or the user explicitly requested an intro). Do not put the order/message in `firstMessage`.
- See AGENTS.md "Human greeting protocol".

# One beat at a time

- `spokenBrief` must be a turn-by-turn guide, never a monologue of stacked questions.
- On the call: one question/statement → wait for reply → next. See AGENTS.md "One beat at a time".

# Name + pronoun fidelity

- "Anna (my brother)" + he/him → always he/him/his. Never guess she/her from the name. Never respell Anna→Ana.
- See AGENTS.md "Name + pronoun fidelity" and `extractCalleeIdentity` in `openai.js`.

# Chat vs phone missions

- Time/weather/facts/"tell me…" are chat (`POST /api/chat`). Never guess the current time — use the server clock (Hyderabad = Asia/Kolkata).
- Remember Home chat history. Only create a mission when the user wants a call/order.

# Real conversation — no instant exits

- Bare "no" / "not joining" without a reason → ask why once, react, then wrap up. Do not instantly "talk later / goodbye".
- Instant accept only when they already gave a reason, answered the full ask, or are clearly rushing off.
- Never "Can you hear me?" after the chat has started or after goodbye.
- See AGENTS.md "Real conversation — when to accept instantly vs ask why" and `HUMAN_CONVERSATION_RULES` in `vapi.js`.
